derstands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Exchanging Opinions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you express an opinion, you give your ideas on a topic.  You can use some inseparable phrasal verbs when you give opinions.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Some phrases we use to give opinions are: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">So you think ...</span>, <span class=\"italic\">Honestly, ...</span>, <span class=\"italic\">I think ...</span>, and  <span class=\"italic\">I guess ...</span><br/><br/>  You use phrasal verbs when you want to be less formal. They are very common in spoken English.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Phrasal Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">get by<br/><br/>get along<br/><br/>get on<br/><br/>get rid of<br/><br/>get around</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"survive<br/><br/>manage<br/><br/>continue<br/><br/>throw away<br/><br/>avoid\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "So you think that we can get by with either.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Honestly, we couldn't get along without a full bag of onions!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I think we have to get on with this. It's getting late.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I guess we should  get rid of these dry onions.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you ask me, there's no getting around this one being a real hit!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Passive Modals and the Imperative to Talk About Food", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use modal verbs to add meaning to other verbs. They come before the dictionary form (Infinitive without 'to') of the main verb.  Modal verbs can add meaning connected with certainty or obligation.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use modal verbs in the passive voice. <br/> You use the passive voice when you want to focus on the receiver of the action, rather than the 'doer' of the action.<br/><br/>   Here is the structure of a passive sentence:<br/><br/>  Subject + to be + past participle<br/><br/>  For example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Spicy rice <span class=\"italic\">is made</span> with Basmati or American rice.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can add a modal verb before the <span class=\"italic\">to be</span>.<br/><br/>  Subject + modal + to be + past participle<br/><br/>  For example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">The spicy rice <span class=\"strong\">can be made</span> with Basmati or American rice.</span><br/><br/>   Here the sentence now has an additional meaning of possibility, thanks to the modal <span class=\"strong\">can</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you are cooking, or talking about how to cook, you can also use the imperative.<br/> The imperative is used when giving directions.<br/> The subject 'you' is understood and left out.<br/><br/>  Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Boil the vegetables</span>. = You boil the vegetables.<br/><br/> By leaving out 'you' the statement becomes stronger and the focus is shifted to the verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The other ingredients can be found in any good restaurant.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The cinnamon sticks ought to be kept in the spice pantry.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It can be left to cook slowly for about 20 minutes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The sultanas and cashews might be stored there as well.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Fry the onions in sunflower oil.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Boil some water.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Add the spices.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Next, pour in the rice. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "fragrant", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having a pleasant smell", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Basmati is more fragrant than American rice.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about making a rice dish.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "either", "type": "name"}, {"content": "one or the other", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(pronoun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: So you think that we can get by with either?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "pod", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the covering for a seed like a bean or pea", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Cardamom pods ought to be kept in the spice pantry.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cinnamon stick", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a common culinary spice that comes from a tree bark", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Cinnamon sticks are commonly used in food preparation.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cardamom", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an aromatic seed coming from a plant of the same name ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Cardamom is used as one of the ingredients for different dishes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cumin", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a seed that is ground and used as a spice ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Cumin seeds ought to be kept in the spice pantry. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to get rid of", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to discard something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I guess we should  get rid of these dry onions.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob02aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to get in", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to enter a place", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Was a new bag here when you got in? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob02aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "tender", "type": "name"}, {"content": "soft or delicate", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Can you tell me how to know it's ready?  It will be tender and a bit dry.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob02aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "splash", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a small amount, especially of a fluid", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Add a splash of wine on the cake.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob02aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With a partner, brainstorm 8 elements that a successful restaurant must have.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Give your list to another group and have them rank the elements in order of importance. One is the lowest and 8 is the highest.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Exchange your list with a couple more groups.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Take the results and make a report.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Give opinions explaining the results.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a short 2-4 minute presentation showing your results.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I set up an independent survey.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I analyze the results.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I create a report and offer an explanation for the results.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I make a short presentation of my findings.", "type": "text"}]}]}